  "sn24.7:0.1": "Linked Discourses 24.7 ",
  "sn24.7:0.2": "1. Stream-Entry ",
  "sn24.7:0.3": "Cause ",
  "sn24.7:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn24.7:1.2": "“Mendicants, when what exists, because of grasping what and insisting on what, does the view arise: ",
  "sn24.7:1.3": "‘There is no cause or reason for the corruption of sentient beings. ",
  "sn24.7:1.4": "Sentient beings are corrupted without cause or reason. ",
  "sn24.7:1.5": "There’s no cause or reason for the purification of sentient beings. ",
  "sn24.7:1.6": "Sentient beings are purified without cause or reason. ",
  "sn24.7:1.7": "There is no power, no energy, no human strength or vigor. ",
  "sn24.7:1.8": "All sentient beings, all living creatures, all beings, all souls lack control, power, and energy. Molded by destiny, circumstance, and nature, they experience pleasure and pain in the six classes of rebirth’?” ",
  "sn24.7:1.9": "“Our teachings are rooted in the Buddha. …” ",
  "sn24.7:2.1": "“When form exists, because of grasping form and insisting on form, the view arises: ",
  "sn24.7:2.2": "‘There is no cause or reason … ",
  "sn24.7:2.3": "they experience pleasure and pain in the six classes of rebirth.’ ",
  "sn24.7:2.4": "When feeling … ",
  "sn24.7:2.5": "perception … ",
  "sn24.7:2.6": "choices … ",
  "sn24.7:2.7": "consciousness exists, because of grasping consciousness and insisting on consciousness, the view arises: ",
  "sn24.7:2.8": "‘There is no cause or reason … ",
